  "ownership": {
    "primary_items": "Append/reserve store raw pointers and do not AddRef. Resource destructor decrements every stored item+4 exactly once in order, calling virtual+0 only when decrement returns0. This establishes one release obligation per successful appended entry; it does not prove registered parsers always return a fresh owned reference.",
    "primary_null_and_duplicates": "Base destructor does not null-check an item before InterlockedDecrement(item+4). Null appended by earlier allocation-failure path is not a safely destructible item. Duplicate pointers incur repeated decrements; caller must supply corresponding reference obligations.",
    "hierarchy": "Append stores the original raw record pointer. Base destructor skips null records; for each nonnull pointer it destroys fields via00b88180 and returns the native pool slot. Hierarchy data words at+4C are numeric references, not item pointers. Duplicate record pointers are not deduplicated and are invalid for unique teardown.",
    "pool": "Record user payload is84h bytes. Destruction reads hidden pool block index at+84h, finds block through01090254, computes signed(record-block)/88h, writes the resulting16-bit slot to block+4400h indexed by the16-bit free count at+4500h, increments that count and lowers earliest available block01090260 if needed. Critical section01090238 brackets the update;01090250 is incremented/decremented. Allocation internals and concurrent pool invariants remain external.",
    "classification": "Derived destructor frees only three list backing allocations and zeroes begin/end/end-cap pointers; no contained-item release. All three verified append fast paths shallow-copy a pointer and do not AddRef. Their growth callees0071b230,0071b2c0,0071b350 remain external, so all-path borrowed insertion is not claimed.",
    "name_cleanup": "Base resource name+8/+C and hierarchy record name+4/+8 pass existing nonnull pointer,length+1,1 to00419cc0 and invoke00bd1510 on the returned manager. Exact native allocation-pool implementation remains external.",
    "resource_manager_hook": "After item releases and before hierarchy destruction, base destructor passes resource+8 name to manager obtained from004c1400 and calls00b801c0. It cannot be erased from a native-equivalent teardown; exact cache/deregistration semantics remain external."
  },
  "reserve_domain": {
    "capacity_policy": "Signed clamp to16; no action if signed capacity already at least requested. Allocate4*clamped request; shallow-copy current signed-positive count; free old backing memory; install new data and capacity; leave count unchanged. Hierarchy append grows only on count==capacity and requests signed max(capacity+16,16).",
    "invalid_or_failure": "No count<=capacity validation, overflow rejection, transactional allocation failure handling or unused-tail initialization. Null checks are on computed destination slots; with null allocation and count>1 later stores can address4,8,... . Allocator throw/null guarantees are outside this packet."
  },
